        "original_id": "20b9694f-cd7e-52c0-9d6b-b3d4b9a6f9d7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Roger Angell; Harry Stephen Keeler\n- Products: Season Ticket: A Baseball Companion; Five Seasons; Late Innings; The Summer Game\n- Organizations: The New Yorker; The New York Times\n- Topics: American essayists; sports writing; baseball; fiction; non-fiction; criticism; mystery; science fiction\n\nFacts:\n- Harry Stephen Keeler was born on November 3, 1890, and he became a prolific but little-known American author of mysteries and science fiction.\n- Roger Angell was born on September 19, 1920, and he is an American essayist known for writing about sports, especially baseball.\n- Roger Angell wrote numerous works of fiction, non-fiction, and criticism.\n- Roger Angell wrote an annual Christmas poem for The New Yorker for many years.\n- The Summer Game, a previous work by Roger Angell, was a New York Times best-seller.\n- Season Ticket: A Baseball Companion is a 1988 book written by Roger Angell.\n- Roger Angell's previous works include Five Seasons, Late Innings, and The Summer Game.\n- Harry Stephen Keeler died on January 22, 1967.",
